17592186479902 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e692ef2-7942-50c0-987c-003e0499c7d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479379} {:answer/id #uuid "5dbb788f-4b96-5fa4-a950-81307ab26f6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pi }^{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479494} {:answer/id #uuid "7ca40bf8-6377-5d1a-9803-7cbf03f171f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479542} {:answer/id #uuid "c35cedf1-0de5-5562-b74c-d3e0a68630e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi +2}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479655} {:answer/id #uuid "fc35db42-0a91-517b-8f1b-307df57fe44c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c35cedf1-0de5-5562-b74c-d3e0a68630e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi +2}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479655} :answer-field/id #uuid "5689c88b-fb4c-5488-beac-e34a9824569a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479772}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc2162e8-e3d2-5905-8722-73fb096c219a" :question/math-academy-id "q-94880" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]$ at $t=1$ given that $∇f(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y\\,i+\\frac{x}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,j$ and $r(t)=({t}^{2}+1)\\,i+t\\,j.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nIn addition, we've been given that\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y\\,i+\\frac{x}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,j.\n$$\n\nFirst, we substitute $x={t}^{2}+1$ and $y=t$ into $∇f(x,y)$ to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t\\,i+\\frac{{t}^{2}+1}{1+{t}^{2}}\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t\\,i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t\\,i+j)\\cdot (2t\\,i+j) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t\\cdot 2t+1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2t\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the above at $t=1,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(1))] & =2(1)\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1+1 \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi +2}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552629 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3300b6f4-a3cb-5719-834a-3ce95f706574" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\left(7 \\pi + 24\\right) e^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552630} {:answer/id #uuid "a173706e-6c6d-5503-aa64-3fbd8adb1d59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\pi e^{\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552659} {:answer/id #uuid "aeb3ce33-88d3-5cf7-ac21-58ac8f8ca664" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9 + 12 \\pi + 4 \\pi^{2} + 4 \\pi^{2} e^{\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552663} {:answer/id #uuid "dac1d9b0-5582-5825-bd06-d6346490288e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\left(3 + 4 \\pi\\right) e^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552671} {:answer/id #uuid "e63ee131-898b-5cf9-a3cf-85e2960cb2c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\left(3 + 2 \\pi\\right) e^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e63ee131-898b-5cf9-a3cf-85e2960cb2c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\left(3 + 2 \\pi\\right) e^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552674} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebe94a29-5154-5b7b-a526-237832ee07d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552675}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "32141bb4-29d3-5922-9dd9-4806a03ebce3" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]$ at $t=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ given that $∇f(x,y)=\\left(y \\left(\\ln{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(x \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\,j$ and $r(t)=\\left(e^{4 t}\\right)\\,i+\\left(\\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)\\,j.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nIn addition, we've been given that\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\left(y \\left(\\ln{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(x \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\,j.\n$$\n\nFirst, we substitute $x=e^{4 t}$ and $y=\\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}$ into $∇f(x,y)$ to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\left(y \\left(\\ln{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(x \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\,j\\Big|_{x=e^{4 t},\\,y=\\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}} \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(4 t + 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(4 t e^{4 t}\\right)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(e^{4 t}\\right)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)\\,j \\\\  & =\\left(4 e^{4 t}\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(\\left(4 t + 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(4 t e^{4 t}\\right)\\,j\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\left(4 e^{4 t}\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)\\,j\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(4 t + 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)\\cdot \\left(4 e^{4 t}\\right)+\\left(4 t e^{4 t}\\right)\\cdot \\left(3 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(16 t e^{4 t} \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 4 e^{4 t} \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)+\\left(12 t e^{4 t} \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =4 \\left(4 t \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 3 t \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) e^{4 t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the above at $t=\\frac{\\pi}{6},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]\\Big|_{t=\\frac{\\pi}{6}} & =4 \\left(4 t \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 3 t \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) e^{4 t}\\Big|_{t=\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{4 \\left(3 + 2 \\pi\\right) e^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}}{3}\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{4 \\left(3 + 2 \\pi\\right) e^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552637 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "745d9116-ef9b-541d-bed2-643d16922eb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552643} {:answer/id #uuid "7f7ba0a8-a6bd-54d4-aa58-70bb7223e88a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552647} {:answer/id #uuid "d7b593eb-f9bf-53ce-bf40-d2147e6f6ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552668} {:answer/id #uuid "f7270bd1-41dc-56f7-a7ef-3f45cc8da6d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11 \\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552677} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4d5919-123f-5fc6-a9a5-dd9a9139bef1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7b593eb-f9bf-53ce-bf40-d2147e6f6ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552668} :answer-field/id #uuid "408c2e1c-f565-56f9-857f-a463bad15c3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "544db47f-5d7f-59fd-ad5d-2e5f814fbc90" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]$ at $t=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$ given that $∇f(x,y)=\\left(2 x + 3 y\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 x + 3 y\\right)\\,j$ and $r(t)=\\left(\\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(\\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)\\,j.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nIn addition, we've been given that\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\left(2 x + 3 y\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 x + 3 y\\right)\\,j.\n$$\n\nFirst, we substitute $x=\\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}$ and $y=\\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}$ into $∇f(x,y)$ to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\left(2 x + 3 y\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 x + 3 y\\right)\\,j\\Big|_{x=\\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)},\\,y=\\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}} \\\\  & =\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)} + 3 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 \\sqrt{2} \\sin{\\left(2 t + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}\\right)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)\\,j \\\\  & =\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)} + 3 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 \\sqrt{2} \\sin{\\left(2 t + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}\\right)\\,j\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)\\,j\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)} + 3 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)+\\left(3 \\sqrt{2} \\sin{\\left(2 t + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(4 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)} + 6 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)+\\left(- 6 \\sqrt{2} \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)} \\sin{\\left(2 t + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =- \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)} + 12 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)} - 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the above at $t=\\frac{\\pi}{8},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]\\Big|_{t=\\frac{\\pi}{8}} & =- \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)} + 12 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)} - 6\\Big|_{t=\\frac{\\pi}{8}} \\\\  & =\\left(5\\right)+\\left(-6\\right) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552639 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cc1cc5c-e1dd-5953-b7f5-350905b76471" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552624} {:answer/id #uuid "5e6f8c29-1da3-56bc-96c5-b8c840c683db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{99}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552640} {:answer/id #uuid "88b2c5c5-e1e9-52ab-9a2a-79c008b14063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552651} {:answer/id #uuid "d9e75bd5-0acb-5f0b-9cae-77eaf5337078" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\f